==English==

===Etymology===
From [[belly]] + [[ache]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'bɛlijeɪk/}}
* {{audio|en-us-bellyache.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[pain]] in the [[belly]], [[stomach]], or [[abdomen]].
#: ''Eating too much candy can give you a '''bellyache'''.''

====Translations====
{{trans-top|pain in the belly, stomach, or abdomen}}
* Dutch: [[buikpijn]] {{m}}
* Esperanto: [[ventrodoloro]]
* Finnish: [[vatsakipu]], [[mahakipu]]
{{trans-mid}}
* French: [[mal au ventre]] {{m}}
* German: [[Bauchschmerzen]] {{f}}, [[Bauchweh]] {{n}}
* Italian: {{t|it|mal di pancia|m}}
* Spanish: [[dolor de barriga]] {{m}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|bellyach|es}}

# To [[complain]] or [[whine]], especially needlessly.
#: ''Quit '''bellyaching''' about the problem and help us fix it.''

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:complain]]

